    [BugFix][MoE] Check routed-expert dimensions for CANN MegaMoE (#17334)
    
    ## What this PR does
    
    Validate CANN MegaMoE against the routed-expert input width for latent
    MoE models such as Kimi K3. Tokens are projected before reaching the
    routed experts, so `routed_expert_hidden_size` is the relevant operator
    dimension. Models without this field retain the existing `hidden_size`
    and `get_hidden_size()` fallbacks.
    
    The regression test uses a synthetic residual width of 8193 and a valid
    routed width of 3584 to prove the check follows the operator input. It
    also rejects an invalid routed width.
    
    The final diff contains only `vllm_ascend/ascend_config.py` and
    `tests/ut/test_ascend_config.py`. Existing MegaMoE selection,
    communicator initialization, SiTU handling, weight preparation, EP
    limits, and buffer calculations are preserved. `mega_moe_max_tokens`
    retains its default 65536 and positive-only validation. There is no
    DSpark-specific workaround in this PR.
    
    ## Testing
    
    - Host `80.5.17.109`, container `B101_1013_k3`, Python 3.11.10,
    installed vLLM 0.30.0.
    - In an isolated source copy of the container-matching baseline
    `7169fcef80c090cbfb1ded913b917a83c981ef87`, retained the
    routed-dimension change and restored the other four previously modified
    files to the baseline.
    - Ran the complete contents of `tests/ut/test_ascend_config.py`,
    `tests/ut/test_ascend_forward_context.py`,
    `tests/ut/ops/test_moe_comm_method.py`,
    `tests/ut/ops/test_fused_moe.py`, and
    `tests/ut/quantization/methods/w4a8/test_w4a8.py` using the project's
    CPU/NPU-mock setup: **349 passed, 14 warnings in 5.94s**.
    - Ruff 0.14.0 lint/format and Python compilation passed for the restored
    files; the retained dimension change previously passed these checks.
    - Serving source files and installed packages were not changed; no
    service was started or stopped.
    - Exact-main UT execution remains blocked by the older container vLLM
    API (`prepare_dcp_local_seq_lens` is absent). The 349-test result is on
    the container-matching baseline, not an exact-main pass. Matching CI
    remains required; NPU/full-model accuracy and performance have not been
    validated by this revision.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
